hey everyone I'm Abbi sharp welcome to  Abby's kitchen the holidays are here  which pretty much translates to a full  month wine and cheese party and trust me  I will never turn down a good glass of  vino and a well curated cheese platter  but sometimes you want something a  little more substantial elegant and with  a little less cheese but still some  cheese guys I'm not getting rid of all  cheese  so I've parted with my friends at corvy  spirit and wines to bring you my four  favorite holiday appetizers to pair with  my four favorite wines let's get started  first up my cherry and caramelized onion  bruschetta I love pairing this with a  Campo Viejo reserva thanks to its  complementary flavors of bold cherry  plum blackberry and peppery vanilla oh  my god it's really good  first I brush slices of whole-grain  baguette with a touch of olive oil and  fleur de sel and bake at 400 until  golden brown next i saute a sweet onion  low and slow until caramelized in a  touch of olive oil before adding in my  sweet cherries honey balsamic vinegar  and a pinch of salt and pepper and of  course the red wine simmer until the  cherries break down and the mixture  looks jammy when it's time to serve I  lay a few thin slices of black plums  onto the toasts top it with some cherry  jam sprinkled on with the crushed  pistachios and finish with a few  shavings of Parmesan cheese  next is my mushroom and ricotta  bruschetta I love pairing this with a  reserve Chardonnay like this one from  Jacobs Creek because it has a nice  creamy texture and I love that the white  peach flavor and the wine really  complements the light ricotta cheese but  it still lets those tasty mushrooms  shine just heat a teaspoon of oil in a  skillet and saute some mushrooms until  golden brown add in the garlic and thyme  leaves and stir for 30 seconds then pour  in the Chardonnay and a pinch of salt  and pepper and simmer until little  liquid evaporates next I smear my toast  with some part skim ricotta cheese top  with some lemon zest add my sauteed  mushrooms and garnish with some fresh  parsley third let's try my Maine Shango  stuffed prosciutto wrapped date these  babies are addictive and so good with a  Cabernet like this one by Buried hope  this wine has a light blackcurrant and  plum flavor that is really yummy with  the sweet dates and I love the tannins  help cut the richness of the prosciutto  and cheese first place a small piece of  manchego cheese into the cavity of a  pitted date before wrapping it a small  piece of prosciutto  they cut 350 degrees for 12 minutes or  until the bacon crisps up and the cheese  begins to gently melt meanwhile I simmer  half a cup of Cabernet in a touch of  honey until reduced to a thick sweet  syrup toss the wrapped dates in the  sauce and serve warm and finally let's  try my poached pear and almond goat's  cheese skewers I love this recipe with a  Sauvignon Blanc like this one by Stone  Lee because the fresh acidity really  stands up well to the tankiness of the  goat's cheese and the passion fruit  flavors of the wine pear nice  with the fruitiness of the pair into a  small saucepan I put the white wine  water honey lemon rind lemon juice  peppercorns in a cinnamon stick and I  simmer until the honey dissolves then I  add in some balls of pears that I cut  with a melon baller and simmer the  mixture until slightly soft but not  falling apart meanwhile I've roll some  reduced fat goat cheese into some small  balls for tossing them in the toasted  sliced almonds and mince dried  cranberries and I fastened a pair ball  and a goat's cheese ball onto some small  toothpicks and enjoy see it tell me that  is not a serious upgrade from your  traditional cheese and crackers with  wine and appetizer pairings like this  you're probably gonna be tough tuned to  hosting a lot more parties come the new  year thanks so much for watching guys  for more healthy holiday ideas and  recipes be sure to subscribe to my  channel and I'll see you next time on  copy's kitchen
 

